; The SHAPE LANGUAGE — Pulse's foundation for saying what a value IS, now a real format-agnostic serde
; split in two so the CORE can be used with NO bson dependency:
;
;   sift_core  (fennec.pulse.sift.core) — the bson-FREE core: the GADT shape, the combinators, the
;     validation gate, the neutral Value model, native relaxed JSON, derived ops, reflection. A
;     standalone serde. Re-exports its internal modules so the plugin can interpret shapes.
;   sift       (fennec.pulse.sift) — the public facade: sift_core PLUS the BSON format (the BSON-tree
;     codec, the zero-copy byte codecs, the extended-JSON bridge, the Mongo query-vocabulary field
;     helpers). fennec uses Sift.* unchanged; the bson dep lives ONLY here.
;
; All pure + jsoo-safe, shared verbatim by server and browser. Methods and collections WORK ON shapes;
; neither owns this.

(library
 (name sift_core)
 (public_name fennec.pulse.sift.core)
 (modules shape value value_json serde value_format json_writer engine derived codec combinators sift_core)
 (libraries base64))

(library
 (name sift)
 (public_name fennec.pulse.sift)
 (modules value_bson cursor bson_engine bson_reader bson_writer sift)
 (libraries sift_core fennec-mongo.bson fennec-mongo.bson_json fennec-mongo.json bigstringaf base64))
